      "body": "### Motivation\n\nWhen a KV connector loads an entire prompt ($ tokens) on a P/D decode instance, vLLM recomputes the last prompt token ( - 1$) in order to sample the first output token.\nHowever,  was previously called using $ as the processed token count, freeing all prefix blocks before  - W + 1$.\nBecause FlashAttention's sliding window query at  - 1$ reads keys from  - W$ through  - 1$, whenever  - W + 1$ is a multiple of , position  - W$ falls on the last slot of a block that was already freed, resulting in the sliding window layer reading the null block.\n\nFixes #65550.\n\n### Proposed Changes\n\nIn , when , adjust  by -1 when calling , preserving the block containing position  - W$ for the recomputed token.\n",
